"Paper cutters are very handy to make precise, clean cuts on paper or thin cardboard. They are very powerful cutters and can cut many sheets at a time. The back edge of the cutter has a ruler attached. This helps to line up the paper, making it square, and also for more accurate measurements. The rest of the board is covered with a grid, which also aids in alignment. The cutter is a long steel blade with a handle on the end.": "2ef61dbcbafc",
"Paper cutters are very handy to make precise, clean cuts on paper or thin cardboard. They are very powerful cutters and can cut many sheets at a time. The back edge of the cutter has a ruler attached. This helps to line up the paper, making it square, and also for more accurate measurements. The rest of the board is covered with a grid, which also aids in alignment. The cutter is a long steel blade with a handle on the end. To use the paper cutter, lift up the cutter blade and insert some paper. Push the paper snuggly against the ruler on the back to keep it square to the blade. Use your left hand to hold the paper in place and then slowly lower the blade. Be sure to keep your fingers away from the cutting edge, as this device could easily cut one right off. When you are finished, make sure that you store the paper cutter with the blade down. This will prevent any unfortunate accidents. Also, make sure that it is out of the reach of curious little hands.": "baa3ed5ecda0",
